From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] data: do not require a native AppStream when cross compiling

data/meson.build generates appstreamcli's own metainfo by running
appstreamcli - the binary being built - so a cross build cannot run it and
the file asks for a second, native copy of AppStream instead:

  data/meson.build:12:4: ERROR: Dependency "appstream" not found
  (tried pkg-config and cmake)

Satisfying that means a full host build of AppStream and, below it, a host
libxmlb, which Buildroot does not carry. That is a large amount of machinery
for one XML file.

The generated file differs from the one in the source tree only by having
release notes folded in from NEWS and translations merged. The source file is
already complete, valid metainfo for the tool, so install it directly when
cross compiling and leave the native path exactly as it was. The two tests
that run appstreamcli go with it; they cannot run in a cross build either.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/data/meson.build
+++ b/data/meson.build
@@ -9,10 +9,20 @@
 
 # Do not rely on an exe wrapper for rel-info, use the system one in that case
 if meson.is_cross_build()
-    dependency('appstream', version: '>=' + as_version, native: true,
-               not_found_message: 'Native appstream required for cross-building')
-    ascli_exe = find_program('appstreamcli', native: true)
-endif
+    # Install the metainfo as it is in the source tree.
+    #
+    # The generated version differs from it in two ways: release notes folded
+    # in from NEWS, and translations merged. Both are produced by running
+    # appstreamcli, which is the thing being built - so a cross build needs a
+    # second, native copy of AppStream, and requiring one makes this file
+    # cost an entire host build of AppStream and everything under it.
+    #
+    # The source file is complete, valid metainfo describing appstreamcli. It
+    # is only missing the changelog and the translated summaries, neither of
+    # which is worth that.
+    install_data('org.freedesktop.appstream.cli.metainfo.xml',
+                 install_dir: metainfo_dir)
+else
 
 # NOTE: We do not translate the release notes on purpose here.
 # If you do want to give translators a chance to translate them,
@@ -41,6 +51,8 @@
            metainfo_i18n]
 )
 
+endif
+
 # install appstream.conf default template
 install_data('appstream.conf',
              install_dir: as_data_installdir)
